<title>USA: Prudential faces $410 mln settlement - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Prudential faces $410 mln settlement - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prudential Insurance Co of America has agreed to pay at least $410 million to settle lawsuits that alleged the company misled policyholders to get them to buy pricier insurance policies, the Wall Street Journal reported.</p>
<p>The class-action settlement is expected to be announced Tuesday, the Journal reported, quoting anonymous sources.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk  (212) 859-1610</p>
